Screen:
| NiceMonMEGA65 V9.9                            the 32-bit NICE CPU of B. Ulmann
| F1 typewriter
|
|  This is the demo in the ROM, which the core runs at power-up. What you type
|  on the keyboard, or send to the debug UART, appears below the blue bar.
|
|  To run your own programs, connect a computer to the debug UART, at
|  2000000 baud, and load and debug them with tools/mon.py. More is at
|  https://github.com/MJoergen/NiceMonMEGA65
| RETURN new line   DEL delete   cursor keys move   CTRL-L clear
|Hello, world!
|aX      Y
|Q1234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456789
|abRde
|x y z
